Z||000000||COUNTIBLIS||02-04-2001||03:23 PM||||Ok looking at the specs from a n/a 3.1 and specs from the turbo 3.1 out of a grand prix, I dont see much of a difference and a problem of just adding the set up to my 3.1.<P>displacement on a n/a 3.1 is 313cc/192 cu in<P>dispalcement on a turbo 3.1 is 191 cu in 3128cc<P>the compression ratio on a n/a 3.1 is 8.9:1<BR>the compression ratio on a turbo 3.1 is 8.7:1<P>ok to me this isnt a big difference, but im just a learner,  what do some of you experienced guys think?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||02-04-2001||03:42 PM||||Count, <BR>Good luck finding parts. GM only made this engine for a year or two. It was replaced by the 3.4 DOHC. I've heard that replacement parts were outrageously expensive, if you can find 'em at all. <BR>Sorry. Please let us know if you find out differently...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||02-05-2001||09:41 AM||||count,<P>There really isn't a huge difference in the set-up between the two.  Why?  GM/McLaren designed the 3.1L Turbo engine for small amounts of boost.  I have a friend with an  89 GP Turbo and a Turbo Regal.  I will see if I can get him to review your question.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||02-06-2001||09:07 AM||||Gents,<P>My buddy sent a response to my questions regarding the differences between the Turbo 3.1 Vs NA 3.1.  <P>"As far as I can recall, there isn't much different between the NA and the Turbo 3.1L.  I know they had hardened steel cranks and I think forged rods.  The Turbo engine has a different block (to accommodate for the Turbo oil galley plug, that's it).  It has a .01" higher deck height to lower the compression by .1.  I can't think of anything else that made it different.  I put the question out on the list however, and if anything comes up in the next few days I will let you know. "<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||14
